build: 2026-06-23 v10.60.0 (rPPG live coaching — turns the lock diagnostics into user guidance)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Continuation of the rPPG line. The Well measurement card no longer shows a flat "Acquiring…" when a finger is on the lens but won't lock — it now shows SPECIFIC, live guidance derived from the same signal diagnostics added in v10.58: "Cover the rear camera + flash" (no finger), "Press a little lighter" (sensor saturating — bright>0.85 or red>0.92, the over-press case from the founder's device log where brightness collapsed 0.40→0.08), "Press gently and hold still" (pulsatile amplitude too weak, amp<0.0008), "Hold still — finding your pulse…" (signal OK, locking), "Locked". This directly raises on-device lock success by coaching better fingertip placement — complementing the v10.58 algorithmic fix (autocorrelation BPM seed) and the v10.59 hot-loop optimizations. New `CameraRPPGBioPublisher.coachingHint` (pure derived state, main-actor) surfaced via measurementControl. Cumulative build: also carries the rPPG lock fix + amp/pk/acf telemetry (v10.58), the O(1) finger-count + vDSP waveform optimizations (v10.59), Live Colabo, meditation streaks, session share, CIE colour, and Transport/Arrangement. 2 code files. Compile gate validates; behaviour device-verified on the founder's next run.
